> This last time, I was a Lvl 10, sacrificing various monsters (like 
> jackals and hobgoblins) generated by a spell book of create monster.

You want bigger monsters. Every corpse has a "value" which depends on
the monster difficulty (rated 1 to 24). Corpses with value below 8 will
do nothing to your god anger. For chaotic gods, this is worse: they
will not be mollified unless the corpse has value 12 or more.

Tigers, leocrottas, stone giants have value 8. Rock trolls, clay golems,
black puddings have value 12. Note that unicorns have a base value of 6
but get a +3 bonus (if not of your alignment or the altar's alignement).


Random monster generation (including zaps of "create monster") will
generate monsters with value up to (DL+XL)/2 (where "DL" is the dungeon
level -- the depth at which you are -- and "XL" is the character level).
If you are, say, at dungeon level 5, and you are a Lvl 10 character,
then you will get monsters with value at most 7.


